## Why This Is Asked
Gauges practical CBA skills for privacy-conscious features that touch user data, emphasizing cost modeling, data minimization, and risk assessment.

## Key Concepts
- On-device processing, data minimization, and opt-in consent
- Batch sizing, compression, and secure transmission
- Cost levers: storage, CPU energy, network, compliance, and hosting
- Go/no-go criteria tied to break-even and risk tolerance

## Code Example
```javascript
function batchEvents(events, batchSize) {
  const batches = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < events.length; i += batchSize) {
    batches.push(events.slice(i, i + batchSize));
  }
  return batches;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate privacy risk post-implementation (DPIA outcomes, audits)?
- What metrics signal a need to adjust batch size or cadence?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to model edge AI costs with privacy constraints, including memory, energy, latency, and rollout economics.

## Key Concepts
- Edge ML cost modeling
- Latency vs. accuracy trade-offs
- Privacy-by-design and consent flows
- Rollout strategy and maintenance plans

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple cost model for edge translation + summarization
function estimateCBA({translatorMB, summarizerMB, words, energyPerWord, latencyPerWord}) {
  const energy = words * energyPerWord;
  const memory = translatorMB + summarizerMB;
  const latency = words * latencyPerWord;
  return { energy, memory, latency };
}
```

